From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Shenk <kevin@avu.nu>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:19:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Translate the INTERVAL operator forms of date
 arithmetic

"date + INTERVAL n unit", "date - INTERVAL n unit" and "INTERVAL n unit +
date" are MySQL's operator spellings of DATE_ADD() and DATE_SUB(). The
parser accepted them and the translator emitted them verbatim, so SQLite
failed on the first token after INTERVAL. They now go through the same
DATETIME() modifier as DATE_ADD()/DATE_SUB(), from one helper. WEEK
becomes 7 DAY as before, and for a non-literal value the multiplication
is emitted as SQL instead of done in PHP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/sqlite/class-wp-mysql-on-sqlite.php   | 101 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 90 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

